<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Menteshe Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Menteshe Bey was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> leader who, in the 1260s and 1270s, led raiders into the Byzantine coastlands of Caria in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, taking the country around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milas">Milas</a>, Pechin and Miletus. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> that bore his name, one of the first Turkish maritime principalities, whose fleets raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> islands until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> finally absorbed it in the 15th century.</p></div>
